{
 "slug": "reading-tap-guard",
 "module": "reading-tap-guard/src/taps",
 "function": "doubleTaps",
 "note": "Each case names its function in fn: doubleTaps(taps, intervalMs) gives the index of each tap that completes a double tap (core rule from Obsidian app.js: release-to-release under the interval, under 30 px apart, press 500 ms or shorter, moved under 30 px; a tap on a control clears the count); effective(action, intervalMs, pro) gives the behavior in effect; normalizeSettings(saved) repairs data.json. The leading number is the spec rule. Reviewed by hand against each input. wordBounds(text, offset) gives the UTF-16 [start, end] of the word at offset for Select the word, or null.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "1 two quick taps at one point are a double tap",
   "fn": "doubleTaps",
   "args": [
    [
     {
      "down": 0,
      "up": 80,
      "x": 100,
      "y": 100,
      "moved": 0,
      "control": false
     },
